From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steffen Persvold <spersvold@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/tiny: ocfb: convert to a full atomic CRTC + primary plane

drm_simple_display_pipe is a shim over the atomic crtc/plane helpers and only
exposes the single primary plane, which blocks adding cursor/overlay planes
later. Inline the shim: split the pipe into an explicit drm_crtc, a primary
drm_plane, a drm_encoder and the existing connector, relocating the callback
bodies unchanged. No functional change.

- The pipe callbacks move verbatim into the new funcs: mode_valid/enable/disable
  -> crtc_helper_funcs (mode_valid/atomic_enable/atomic_disable); check/update ->
  plane_helper_funcs (atomic_check/atomic_update); enable_vblank/disable_vblank ->
  crtc_funcs. A new crtc atomic_check mirrors what drm_simple_display_pipe did
  internally (check_crtc_primary_plane when enabled + add_affected_planes).
  prepare_fb = drm_gem_plane_helper_prepare_fb; crtc/plane state via the default
  atomic helpers (no new per-object state).
- The flip event is still armed by the plane atomic_update / the DMA-done IRQ
  resolve; there is deliberately no crtc atomic_flush (which would double-arm).
- All &pipe.crtc / &pipe.plane sites retarget to &ocfb->crtc / &ocfb->primary
  (vblank handling, flip resolve, damage clips, the vsync IRQ handler).

Structural prerequisite for driver-side plane composition; adds no planes and no
behaviour of its own.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/ocfb-drm.c | 200 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 149 insertions(+), 51 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/ocfb-drm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/ocfb-drm.c
index d6b02c4a..0143dcd9 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/ocfb-drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/ocfb-drm.c
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
  * The hardware is a single-plane scanout engine: an AXI master DMA-reads a
  * contiguous framebuffer and drives an RGB/HDMI output with programmable
  * display timing. There is no overlay, cursor or acceleration, so it maps
- * onto drm_simple_display_pipe + GEM-DMA, with fbdev emulation bringing the
+ * onto a full atomic CRTC + GEM-DMA, with fbdev emulation bringing the
  * console back.
  *
  * An optional companion DMA command engine enables "copy-on-flip": userspace
@@ -48,24 +48,28 @@
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 
 #include <drm/clients/drm_client_setup.h>
+#include <drm/drm_atomic.h>
 #include <drm/drm_atomic_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_connector.h>
+#include <drm/drm_crtc.h>
 #include <drm/drm_damage_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_device.h>
 #include <drm/drm_drv.h>
 #include <drm/drm_edid.h>
+#include <drm/drm_encoder.h>
 #include <drm/drm_fb_dma_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_fbdev_dma.h>
 #include <drm/drm_fourcc.h>
 #include <drm/drm_framebuffer.h>
+#include <drm/drm_gem_atomic_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_gem_dma_helper.h>
